---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { site } from '../consts';
---

<Section id="work" title="Current work">
  <p>
    SSCCS is an entirely new computing model and a hardware architecture, so the research is
    ongoing. What runs today is the infrastructure stack, on the silicon and the computing models
    in use now, and each layer that runs tests another part of the model against a working system.
  </p>

  <p>
    The work also runs in the other direction. Products, and the infrastructure elements that
    support them, are implemented and composed first, and what they require is what moves the model
    forward.
  </p>

  <dl class="defs">
    <dt>Field composition algebra</dt>
    <dd>
      The current focus of the core team. Constraint sets have to compose while observation
      determinism is preserved, so that a composed Field can be reasoned about with the same
      guarantees as its parts.
    </dd>

    <dt>Compiler pipeline</dt>
    <dd>
      The core compiler and runtime are under active development, with work on{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/research/rust_baremetal.html">compiler pipeline hardening</a>{' '}
      and on <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/research/riscv.html">hardware mapping</a>, including
      the decode path that replaces a hash unit with combinational logic.
    </dd>

    <dt>Domain instantiations</dt>
    <dd>
      The model is carried into the field by projects held by separate entities, which the foundation
      supplies with the open-source technology and works alongside. The commercial ones among them
      stand on their own, so the stack does not depend on a single source of support.
    </dd>

    <dt>Hardware validation</dt>
    <dd>
      Phased prototyping from software emulation to FPGA deployment, with a parallel track for
      radiation-tolerant platforms. See{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/works/openhw_integration.html">hardware validation</a>.
    </dd>

    <dt>Strategic partnerships</dt>
    <dd>
      Work with infrastructure leaders to extend the reach of agentic research environments, and
      contribution to established open-source projects, whose requirements come back into the
      research as constraints the model has to meet. There is a standing invitation to institutions
      that want to validate the model against their own workloads.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <p>
    The <a href={site.works}>work notes</a> carry the measurements behind each of these as they are
    taken.
  </p>
</Section>
